# Internal working documents stay local; the shipped ones are allow-listed.
#
# This block is a trap and has already sprung once, on Grid: a document was
# written, committed with a message saying so, and was not on GitHub for a day,
# because it was not on the list and `git add` had nothing to add. Adding a
# document here is half the job — `scripts/doc-check.sh` asserts each required
# document is actually *tracked*, which is the half that catches it.
docs/*
!docs/00-PRODUCT-STATEMENT.md
!docs/ROADMAP.md
!docs/JOURNAL.md
!docs/FEATURE-BACKLOG.md
!docs/adr/
!docs/screenshots/

# OS / editors
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.log

# Node / React Native
node_modules/
.expo/
*.jsbundle
ios/Pods/
ios/build/
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
.env
.env.local

# Build output and task cache
dist/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# .NET
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
*.user
